          "message": "feat(orchestration): retriage cron, migration gating pre-flight, paginated readiness snapshot (#2467)\n\nAudit fix wave (audit-2026-07-17), sparq-side items:\n\n- retriage.yml + scripts/retriage.py: status:untriaged was TERMINAL (triage only fires on\n  opened/edited/reopened; the edited event does not cover label changes). The */30 cron re-runs\n  the same static triage over parked untriaged issues by trusted authors, applying a default\n  priority:P3 only when NO priority label exists (ambiguity still parks for a human); epics and\n  trust:untrusted are excluded.\n- bd-to-issues.py migration pre-flight: map blocked:*/blocked-on-* -> needs:* gates (drop\n  blocked-by-epic:*); gate external/audit beads (sq-qhy4 class, token-placement, maintainer\n  decisions) as needs:user so the deferred-retry loop can never re-fire them; pre-create the FULL\n  label set (ensure_labels) and FAIL LOUDLY on issue-create errors instead of the silent\n  drop-all-labels fallback that produced permanently-untriaged, partition-less issues.\n- ready-issues.py: real cursor pagination (gh api --paginate) replaces the 1000-issue fail-closed\n  cliff that the full 893-bead migration would have tripped; explicit runaway ceiling retained.\n- research/context-economy-worker-fleet.md: pilot E (hook-firing canary) RESULT — the committed\n  PreToolUse sparq-perf-reviewer agent hook does NOT fire in fresh-HOME headless worker runs with\n  today's settings, but agent hooks DO run headless in general (config-interaction suppression,\n  not a guarantee); matcher hardening stays a follow-up.\n\nSelf-tests extended (non-vacuous) in retriage.py, bd-to-issues.py, ready-issues.py; workflow\nactionlint/yaml clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
