          "message": "feat(ci): draft-tier CI — reduced matrix on draft PR heads, full-tier supersession at ready_for_review (#2537)\n\n* feat(ci): draft-tier CI — reduced matrix on draft PR heads, full-tier supersession at ready_for_review\n\nDraft pull_request heads now run only the change-scoped crate legs (the\nexisting ci-select intersection), the cheap global gates, and the\nci-summary gate over exactly that reduced set; coverage, benchmarks\n(+ per-PR bench comments), CodeQL, the heavy recall shards, and the\nwasm artifact-exact-equality leg (unless the sparq-wasm closure is\naffected) are skipped. Non-draft heads, merge_group, push-to-main and\nschedule are byte-identical to before, and no required-check name\nchanges (the ruleset still requires exactly `ci-summary / gate`).\n\nIntegrity invariant — a draft-tier gate result can never admit a PR to\nthe merge queue (scripts/ci_summary_gate.py, unit-tested):\n* every gate-feeding workflow adds ready_for_review to its\n  pull_request types, so un-drafting re-runs the FULL matrix on the\n  same head SHA and the fresh gate supersedes the draft-tier one;\n* the ci-select job name carries a \", draft-tier\" marker on\n  draft-assembled runs; a full-tier PR gate holds (still-settling) and\n  then REDs (\"stale draft-tier run, full run pending\") while a\n  draft-marked select has no later full-tier successor;\n* a draft-tier gate re-reads the PR's CURRENT draft state via the API\n  before any SUCCESS and REDs if the PR was un-drafted (API failure\n  fail-closes to RED);\n* cancelled/stale check-runs left on the SHA by the ready_for_review\n  concurrency cancel are excused only when a later same-normalized-name\n  run exists — genuine failures are never forgiven.\n\nAlso: per-PR cancel-in-progress concurrency for bench pull_request runs\n(push/schedule still never cancel — history integrity) and js.yml;\ndocs/branch-protection.md gains the §Draft-tier CI design record.\n\nMotivation (measured, 2026-07-17): 12-17 draft worker PRs cycling\nreview-fix rounds, ~100-200 checks per push, 52 concurrent runs + 8\nqueued saturating the org pool — heads yellow 30+ min, gates timing out\nas false failures, the merge queue starving.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): close the draft-tier gate supersession window + per-instance select supersession\n\nCritic-round fixes for the two blocking defects on the draft-tier CI design:\n\n1. GATE INTEGRITY — a concluded draft-tier `gate` SUCCESS used to remain the\n   LATEST run of the required context from the un-draft moment until the\n   ready_for_review ci-summary run registered its check-run (seconds of event\n   latency; indefinitely on a dropped event or an Actions outage), and\n   `gh pr ready && gh pr merge --auto` could enqueue inside that window — with\n   the merge_group run deliberately excluding bench's deterministic ratchet +\n   the heavy recall shards (sq-6vshe.6). Fixed STRUCTURALLY: the ci-summary\n   gate job's own check-run name is now tiered (`gate, draft-tier` on draft\n   payloads, exactly `gate` everywhere else), so a draft-tier run never\n   produces the required context at all — branch protection blocks on the\n   ABSENT check, closing the latency, event-loss and TOCTOU variants at once.\n   scripts/ci_summary_gate.py treats stale `gate, draft-tier` check-runs as\n   tier artifacts (excluded from every sibling set — a completed draft-tier\n   FAILURE can no longer permanently RED the full-tier gate on the same SHA).\n   docs/branch-protection.md: the factually-wrong worst-race paragraph is\n   replaced with the structural argument, and the ruleset's `code_scanning`\n   rule is recorded (and wiring-tested) as defense-in-depth only — an\n   out-of-repo, owner-mutable, evadable setting, never load-bearing.\n\n2. Cross-workflow select-name collision — ci.yml, bench.yml,\n   feature-matrix.yml and fuzz.yml expose the IDENTICAL select check-run name,\n   so the old name-matched belt let the FIRST full-tier select to register\n   supersede ALL FOUR draft-marked selects, releasing the hold while the other\n   workflows' full-tier runs had registered nothing. draft_selects_unsuperseded\n   now requires a distinct, strictly-later full-tier successor PER draft-select\n   INSTANCE (greedy start-order matching within each normalized-name group,\n   duplicates preserved for count reporting); an unsatisfiable hold REDs at\n   budget exhaustion (fail-closed), never passes over draft-assembled legs.\n\nTests: test_ci_summary_gate.py 56/56 (new: per-instance supersession incl. the\n1-of-4 collision regression, gate-artifact exclusion incl. the non-vacuous\ndraft-gate-FAILURE case, tie-break ordering); test_ci_select_wiring.py 50/50\n(gate name = 'gate' + marker expression pinned in both renderings, code_scanning\nbackstop triggers + doc wording). actionlint: zero new findings; typos clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
